{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":23,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.QCubicEqBindingKernel.cubic_lead_eq_kernel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.QCubicEqBindingKernel.cubic_lead_eq_kernel","kind":"theorem","line":311,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.lean#L311-L311","doc":"For any DM q-cubic `c` of `F` (any cubic realising the period differential),\nthere is a distinguished base direction `d` whose self-contraction is the\n**nonzero** binding-kernel leading weight: `c_{ddd} = κ ≠ 0`.  The open\nidentification of the geometric q-cubic with the C1 kernel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.QCubicEqBindingKernel.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.QCubicEqBindingKernel.mk","kind":"ctor","line":305,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.lean#L305-L305","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.QCubicEqBindingKernel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.QCubicEqBindingKernel","kind":"class","line":274,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.lean#L274-L314","doc":"**§3b dependent target conjecture class — the q-cubic equals the binding\nkernel C1.**\n\n`@conjecture: dependent` (depends on `QDonagiMarkmanCubicCondition F` via the\n`[Instance]` binder — the dependency edge, §3b-tax).\n\n**THIS IS THE GENUINE OPEN WALL.**  It asserts the identity that would give\nthe keystone binding kernel **C1** an *independent geometric origin*: the\nDonagi–Markman q-cubic `c` of the Bring q-Lagrangian fibration `F` (which\nexists by `[QDonagiMarkmanCubicCondition F]`) equals the binding kernel C1 —\nconcretely, `c` has a distinguished base direction `d` whose self-contraction\n`c_{ddd}` is the **nonzero** leading recurrence-kernel weight\n`κ = QOU.Machinery.QProlongation.recurrenceKernelLead` (the top-shift term of\nthe proved depth-2 C1 kernel `[n+2]_q b_{n+2} = b_{n+1} + b_n`,\n`QOU.Mass.QDifferenceConfluentObstruction`).\n\n**Honesty.**  `κ` is carried abstractly (documented contract, mirroring\n`QOU.Mathlib.QJetBundle`'s light-import discipline) rather than importing the\nheavy `QuantumTorus` cone; the class names the exact decls it stands for.\nThe field is content-bearing (a nonzero leading identification in the shape of\nthe claim), NOT a marker.  **No instance is supplied.**  If this identity were\n*derived* (not fitted) it would de-tautologize QDM-3 — but it is NOT proved\nhere.  The earlier `symbol D_q = recurrenceKernelLead κ` is a tautological\nre-encoding of the recurrence; nothing above supplies the independent\ngeometric side, and this class must NOT be discharged by a fit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.categorical_lagrangian_dm_cubic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.categorical_lagrangian_dm_cubic","kind":"theorem","line":234,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.lean#L234-L270","doc":"**Conditional on `QDonagiMarkmanCubicCondition F` and\n`BringHolomorphicSymplectic D`** (both taken as explicit `[Instance]`\nhypotheses — the binders ARE the dependency edges, §3b-tax): applying the\nDonagi–Markman cubic condition to the Bring q-Lagrangian fibration `F`\n(whose base is Lagrangian for `Ω_ℂ` by `D`) yields a q-cubic `c` on the base\nthat\n\n* reproduces the period differential (`∂_k τ_{ij} = c_{ijk}`), and\n* is fully `S₃`-symmetric — here witnessed by the 3-cycle symmetry\n  `c_{ijk} = c_{jki}`, **derived** by composing the two transposition\n  symmetries of the class (a genuine composition of the class fields, not a\n  self-assuming projection), and\n\nwhile the wavefront stays isotropic for `Ω_ℂ` (carried through from `D`).\n\nThis is a §3b-cond *rigorous conditional result*: fully verified by Lean\nmodulo the two named, class-axiomatised conjectural inputs.  It does **NOT**\nidentify `c` with the binding kernel — that is the separate open target\n`QCubicEqBindingKernel` below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.BringHolomorphicSymplectic.wavefront_half_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.BringHolomorphicSymplectic.wavefront_half_dim","kind":"theorem","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.lean#L229-L229","doc":"The on-shell wavefront is half-dimensional: it carries exactly `dim/2`\nindependent directions (the completing half of \"Lagrangian\"). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.BringHolomorphicSymplectic.wavefront_isotropic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.BringHolomorphicSymplectic.wavefront_isotropic","kind":"theorem","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.lean#L225-L225","doc":"The on-shell wavefront is isotropic: `Ω_ℂ` restricts to `0` on it (the\ndefining half of \"Lagrangian\"). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.BringHolomorphicSymplectic.omega_nondegenerate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.BringHolomorphicSymplectic.omega_nondegenerate","kind":"theorem","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.lean#L222-L222","doc":"`Ω_ℂ` is non-degenerate: every tangent direction pairs non-trivially. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.BringHolomorphicSymplectic.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.BringHolomorphicSymplectic.mk","kind":"ctor","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.lean#L219-L219","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.BringHolomorphicSymplectic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.BringHolomorphicSymplectic","kind":"class","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.lean#L195-L230","doc":"**§3b primary conjecture class — the Bring holomorphic-symplectic 2-form and\nthe Lagrangian wavefront.**\n\n`@conjecture: primary`\n\nThe Bring hyperkähler cone carries a **non-degenerate** holomorphic-symplectic\n2-form `Ω_ℂ` (the `omega` of `D`), and the on-shell categorical-Lagrangian\nwavefront `𝒟_∇ψ = 0` (`D.onShell`) is **Lagrangian** with respect to it:\nisotropic (`Ω_ℂ` restricts to `0`) and half-dimensional.\n\n**The 4-form → 2-form correction is the reason this class exists.**  On the\nreal-4-dim Bring cone the tetraplectic 4-form degenerates to a volume form and\ncarries no fibration data; the holomorphic-symplectic 2-form `Ω_ℂ` (signalled\nby the 3-Sasakian link + the Reeb twist `[M_i,M_j] = 2M_k`,\n`QOU.Tetraplectic.BringCone`) is the load-bearing structure.\n\n**Content (not a marker).**  Three parameter-quantified fields: global\nnon-degeneracy, isotropy of the wavefront, and half-dimensionality — together\nexactly \"the wavefront is a Lagrangian submanifold of `(·, Ω_ℂ)`\".  No\ninstance is supplied — the honest open state. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.QDonagiMarkmanCubicCondition.exists_cubic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.QDonagiMarkmanCubicCondition.exists_cubic","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.lean#L187-L187","doc":"There is a totally-symmetric cubic `c` realising the period differential:\n`c` is symmetric under the (1 2) and (2 3) transpositions (which generate\n`S₃`), and `∂_k τ_{ij} = c_{ijk}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.QDonagiMarkmanCubicCondition.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.QDonagiMarkmanCubicCondition.mk","kind":"ctor","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.lean#L182-L182","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.QDonagiMarkmanCubicCondition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.QDonagiMarkmanCubicCondition","kind":"class","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.lean#L159-L191","doc":"**§3b primary conjecture class — the q-Donagi–Markman cubic condition.**\n\n`@conjecture: primary`\n\nThe q-analogue of the Donagi–Markman cubic condition\n(`[donagi-markman1996cubics]` §1): for the q-Lagrangian fibration `F`, there\nis a **field of totally-symmetric cubics** `c ∈ Sym³ T*B` — symmetric under\nevery transposition of its three slots — whose contraction reproduces the\ndifferential of the q-period map, `dPeriod = ⟨c, ·⟩` (i.e. `∂_k τ_{ij} =\nc_{ijk}`).\n\n**Content (not a marker).**  `F` records only that `dPeriod` is symmetric in\nits first two slots (the period matrix is symmetric).  The class asserts the\nSTRONGER, non-automatic fact that `dPeriod` is *totally* symmetric — the\nintegrability equivalent to `τ` being a Hessian `∂²F` and the fibration being\nLagrangian (an ACIHS).  This is FALSE for a generic `dPeriod`, so the class\ngenuinely constrains `F`; it is not dischargeable for an arbitrary fibration.\n\nNo instance is supplied — the honest open state of the cubic-condition\nconjecture. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.BringHKData.onShell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.BringHKData.onShell","kind":"def","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.lean#L155-L155","doc":"The on-shell categorical-Lagrangian wavefront `𝒟_∇ψ = 0`, as a family of\ntangent directions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.BringHKData.omega_antisymm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.BringHKData.omega_antisymm","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.lean#L152-L152","doc":"`Ω_ℂ` is antisymmetric. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.BringHKData.omega","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.BringHKData.omega","kind":"def","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.lean#L150-L150","doc":"The holomorphic-symplectic 2-form `Ω_ℂ` (a bilinear form on the tangent\nmodel). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.BringHKData.dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.BringHKData.dim","kind":"def","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.lean#L147-L147","doc":"Real dimension of the tangent model (even, for a symplectic form). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.BringHKData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.BringHKData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.lean#L145-L145","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.BringHKData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.BringHKData","kind":"structure","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.lean#L138-L155","doc":"**Bring hyperkähler / holomorphic-symplectic data.**  The tangent model of\nthe Bring cone carries an antisymmetric 2-form `omega = Ω_ℂ` (the\nholomorphic-symplectic form — the load-bearing structure after the\n4-form → 2-form correction) and a predicate `onShell` selecting the on-shell\ncategorical-Lagrangian wavefront directions `𝒟_∇ψ = 0`.  Non-degeneracy and\nthe Lagrangian property of `onShell` are the *conjectural* content and live\nin `BringHolomorphicSymplectic`, not here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.QLagrangianFibration.dPeriod_symm_ij","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.QLagrangianFibration.dPeriod_symm_ij","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.lean#L136-L136","doc":"The q-period matrix is symmetric: `∂_k τ_{ij} = ∂_k τ_{ji}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.QLagrangianFibration.dPeriod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.QLagrangianFibration.dPeriod","kind":"def","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.lean#L134-L134","doc":"Differential of the q-period map: `dPeriod i j k = ∂_k τ_{ij}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.QLagrangianFibration.dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.QLagrangianFibration.dim","kind":"def","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.lean#L132-L132","doc":"Complex dimension of the fibration base `B`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.QLagrangianFibration.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.QLagrangianFibration.mk","kind":"ctor","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.lean#L130-L130","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.QLagrangianFibration","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.QLagrangianFibration","kind":"structure","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/CategoricalLagrangianDMCubic.lean#L123-L136","doc":"**q-Lagrangian fibration data.**  A base of dimension `dim` together with the\n*differential of the (q-)period map* `dPeriod i j k = ∂_k τ_{ij}`, where\n`τ_{ij}` is the (symmetric) q-period matrix.  We record only the symmetry the\nperiod matrix carries a priori — symmetry in the first two slots\n(`τ_{ij} = τ_{ji}`).  The *third-slot* symmetry is exactly the Donagi–Markman\ncubic condition and is therefore NOT recorded here — it is the content of the\nconjecture class `QDonagiMarkmanCubicCondition`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}